# Ontology Lab: On a Project for Creating a New Type of AI

**An Essay-Synopsis**

**Serge Magomet (Aimate)**
Independent Researcher
Ontology Lab

2026

---

## Abstract

This working paper presents an essay-synopsis of a project to create an original AI model built on an ontological pattern developed within Ontology Lab (2025–2026). The pattern comprises four axioms (unbounded ontological regimes, absolute connectivity, paradoxical stability, scale asymmetry), 36+1 properties, transition operators, and a complexity metric. Unlike existing LLMs, the proposed model can hold paradoxes without collapse, treat boundaries as translation zones, exercise functional reflexivity, conduct dialogue as co-inquiry, and preserve meaning across ontological regimes. The claims are offered as a working hypothesis, not metaphysical dogma. The project is considered along two horizons: the constitution of a "new human"—the operational human—and the creation of an AI with a different architecture of cognition. It invites critical dialogue and collaboration.

**Keywords:** Ontology Lab, MPO-System, dynamic realism, Superreality, ontological pattern, AI architecture, paradoxical stability, operational phenomenology, cross-domain translation, ontological recalibration, co-inquiry, symbiogenesis

**JEL Classification:** B59, O31, O33, O34, Z19

