## Key Concepts at a Glance

| Term | Brief Definition |
|------|------------------|
| **Superreality** | A unified field of absolute connectivity, encompassing an unbounded multiplicity of ontological regimes. |
| **Ontological regime** | A type of reality possessing its own laws and irreducible to others. |
| **Paradoxical stability** | The capacity of a system to preserve its integrity in the presence of contradictions. |
| **Scale asymmetry** | Movement "inward" has a limit; movement "outward" has none. |
| **Salience** | A measure of how far a pattern is capable of changing a system. |
| **Interfaceness** | The capacity to use boundaries as zones of translation. |
| **Emanation / embodiment** | The mutual actualization of patterns between ontological layers. |
| **Operational phenomenology** | A method for studying experience without reducing it to physiology or metaphysics. |

*(A full glossary is provided in Appendix A of the paper.)*

